---
title: ONI strings
tags: tools
heading: "Extract strings"
summary: >-
    Pulls out the runs of printable characters in a string that are at least a set length.
---
{% from "macros/tool.njk" import toolSection with context %}
{% from "macros/tool-frame.njk" import toolFrame %}
{% set filename = page.fileSlug %}
{% set intro %}
    <p>Useful for finding text hidden in data, such as a file decoded from Base64: printable characters are the letters, digits, punctuation and spaces of plain ASCII. The minimum length is a whole number of at least 1, and runs shorter than it are left out.</p>
    <p>Strings lists the runs, one per line. Positions puts where each starts before it, counting characters from 0, so it can be found again in the input.</p>
    <p>In the browser console: <code class="tool-example">convrtr.{{ filename }}(string, n = 4)</code> gives the runs, and <code class="tool-example">convrtr.findStrings(string, n = 4)</code> gives each with its position.</p>
{% endset %}
{% call toolSection(intro) %}
{% call toolFrame(filename, "Extract strings", placeholder = "Example: ÿØÿàJFIF¤Hello there¶ü", tabs = ["Strings", "Positions"], actions = [{ id: filename + "Run", label: "Extract" }]) %}
<div class="tool-field tool-field--short">
    <label class="tool-field__label" for="{{ filename }}Min">Minimum length</label>
    <input type="number" class="form-control" id="{{ filename }}Min" autocomplete="off" min="1" value="4" aria-describedby="{{ filename }}Status">
</div>
{% endcall %}
{% endcall %}
